What follows Kira's source, by file:
  parallel_kira_gen.py
    read_system_eqs, and the file naming and SYSTEMconfig handling in merge:
      the SYSTEM_*.gz loader, src/kira/reductionFF.cpp (Kira::load_ff_system),
      and the writer, src/kira/kira.cpp
    emit_top, block writer and token order:  src/kira/kira.cpp
    emit_top, preferred-master weights:      src/pyred/integrals.cpp
                                             (Integral::set_preferred_masters)
    emit_top, operator templates:            src/pyred/relations.cpp
  parallel_kira_gen_uds.py
    FAM_RE, AI_RE, load_ops:                 src/pyred/relations.cpp
                                             (import of the IBP and LI files)
    gen_sector, substitution of seed indices: src/pyred/relations.cpp
                                             (IntegralRelations::sow_ibp_streq)
No block is a copy or a statement-by-statement translation of Kira's code.
The scripts reproduce formats and conventions that Kira's source states and
Kira's papers do not. The sharding by cover tops, the synthetic targets, the
union and deduplication in merge, the launcher, the probe, the monomial parser
and the seed enumeration were written for BootLoops.

selftest.py and the flat aliases tools/parallel_kira_gen.py and
tools/parallel_kira_gen_uds.py load the two GPL scripts; a program that loads
them is a combined work offered under GPL-3.0-or-later terms. The top-emit
route also loads pyred_weight.py, a GPL-3.0-or-later tool shipped in the
sibling repository kira (bootloops-tools/). build_restage.py and
kira_gpl_tools.py do not load either script and remain usable on their own
under MIT.

